"""distcc-mirror: set up and run distcc's mirrored-tree mode.

One config file per project (~/.config/distcc-mirror/<name>.conf) holds
everything: the source roots, the build directory, the helpers.  The
commands below read it, so no environment variables have to be set by hand.

Getting started, on the machine that runs the builds:

  contrib/distcc-mirror install --helper m6       build, install here and on m6
  distcc-mirror init --helper m6 --build build    write the project's config
  distcc-mirror helper install                    start the daemon on m6 (LaunchAgent)
  distcc-mirror doctor                            check both machines match
  distcc-mirror build                             PCHs, sync, ninja

Commands:
  install      build distcc from this source tree, install it here and on
               the helpers
  init         write a config for a project
  show         print the config and the environment it gives
  env          print export lines:  eval "$(distcc-mirror env)"
  run CMD...   run a command with that environment
  shell        start a shell with that environment
  sync         copy the tree to the helpers (distcc --mirror-sync)
  build        build PCHs, sync, then run ninja (or make)
  test         compile a few files through the mirror and compare the
               objects with local compiles
  doctor       check the setup on this machine and the helpers
  helper       install/start/stop/restart/status/log/uninstall the helper
               daemon
  brew-parity  compare Homebrew between this machine and the helpers, and
               copy missing kegs

Run "distcc-mirror COMMAND --help" for the options of each command.
"""

